WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.815
Use mission and asset identifiers in file names and folders.

00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:08.140
Organize originals, working products, annotations, maps, defect records, reports,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.083
and exports separately.

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:13.090
Preserve the relationship between every reported observation and its source file.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:18.035
Metadata may include time, position, aircraft, sensor, camera settings, altitude estimate,

00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:19.041
and processing history.

00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:20.760
Preserve it where appropriate,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.730
but validate location after navigation anomalies and avoid treating metadata as

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.520
infallible.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.695
Inspection notes should describe asset component, observation, evidence reference,

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:32.183
environmental context, confidence, and recommended follow-up.

00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:36.535
Defect tags organize review but should not imply engineering severity unless a qualified

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:37.348
authority assigns it.

00:00:37.348 --> 00:00:41.400
G I S integration can connect observations with approved asset layers and repeat

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.070
inspections.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.960
Check coordinate reference, accuracy, asset identifiers, and map currency.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.904
A precise symbol can still be attached to uncertain source data.

00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:53.120
Reports distinguish direct observation, automated detection, analyst judgment,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.360
and specialist conclusion.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.080
Include overview and close-up evidence, limitations, missing coverage,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.800
collection conditions, and what additional inspection is needed.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.020
Infrastructure data can reveal layout, condition, access routes, vulnerabilities,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.400
and operational details.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.300
Apply access control, encryption and secure transfer where appropriate, backup, retention,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.035
controlled sharing, and review before public release.

00:01:14.035 --> 00:01:15.905
Version reports and correction records.

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:18.360
If a component label, location, interpretation,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.499
or severity changes after specialist review,

00:01:20.499 --> 00:01:25.100
preserve the superseded conclusion and explain the update so downstream teams do not act

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.030
on stale findings.
